ilename -> list of extracted items\\n  - Each item has: item_name_raw, source_file, source_page/source_row\\n\\nMake all code clean, with type hints, docstrings, and proper error handling. Use pathlib.Path for all file paths. Print progress messages in Arabic.\",\n    \"inherit\": true,\n    \"model\": \"MODEL_PLACEHOLDER_M26\",\n    \"modelTier\": \"MODEL_TIER_INHERIT\"\n  },\n  \"result\": {\n    \"conversationId\": \"218cbc5d-e25c-452d-99ba-3004c6d3e6f6\",\n    \"logAbsoluteUri\": \"file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/218cbc5d-e25c-452d-99ba-3004c6d3e6f6/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl\",\n    \"workspaceUris\": [\n      \"file:///d%3A/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"spec\": {\n    \"typeName\": \"pharmacy-builder\",\n    \"role\": \"Match and output builder\",\n    \"initialPrompt\": \"Create the following files for the pharmacy drug matching project at d:\\\\AI_Engineer\\\\Pharmacy-agy:\\n\\n## 1. src/match/__init__.py (empty)\\n\\n## 2. src/match/text_match.py\\nText preprocessing and fuzzy matching module:\\n\\n```python\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Text cleaning and fuzzy matching for Arabic drug names.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n```\\n\\nFunctions:\\n- normalize_text(text: str) -> str:\\n  - Convert Arabic-Indic digits (٠-٩) to Western digits (0-9)\\n  - Remove tatweel/kashida (ـ)\\n  - Remove tashkeel/diacritics\\n  - Normalize whitespace (multiple spaces to single)\\n  - Strip leading/trailing whitespace\\n  - Normalize different forms of alef (أ, إ, آ -> ا)\\n  - Normalize taa marbuta (ة -> ه) for search purposes\\n  - DO NOT remove any words, abbreviations, or numbers\\n  - Return normalized text\\n\\n- find_candidates(query: str, items: list[str], threshold: float = 0.60, max_results: int = 5) -> list[tuple[str, float]]:\\n  - Normalize both query and items\\n  - Use rapidfuzz.fuzz.token_sort_ratio for scoring\\n  - Also try rapidfuzz.fuzz.partial_ratio and take the max\\n  - Return top matches above threshold as list of (original_item, score)\\n  - Score is 0-100 from rapidfuzz, we normalize to 0-1\\n\\n- quick_match(query: str, item: str) -> float:\\n  - Quick similarity score between two drug names\\n  - Returns 0.0 to 1.0\\n\\n## 3. src/match/gemini_match.py\\nGemini-based intelligent drug matching:\\n\\n```python\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Use Gemini to resolve ambiguous drug name matches.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n```\\n\\nFunctions:\\n- match_with_gemini(shortage_name: str, candidates: list[dict], api_key: str, model: str = 'gemini-2.5-flash') -> dict:\\n  - Takes a shortage drug name and list of candidate items from a warehouse\\n  - Each candidate has: item_name_raw, source (filename)\\n  - Sends to Gemini with a carefully crafted prompt\\n  - The prompt asks Gemini to:\\n    1. Compare the shortage drug name with each candidate\\n    2. Consider: drug name, concentration/strength, dosage form, pack size\\n    3. Return a JSON with: matched_index (or -1 if no match), confidence (high/medium/low), reason\\n    4. If there's a clear match (same drug, same strength, same form) -> match\\n    5. If drug name matches but strength/form differs -> no match\\n    6. If ambiguous -> return confidence=low\\n  - Uses google.genai client (the new SDK)\\n  - Uses structured output (response_mime_type='application/json')\\n  - Returns: {\\\"matched\\\": bool, \\\"matched_item\\\": str|None, \\\"confidence\\\": str, \\\"reason\\\": str}\\n\\n- batch_match_with_gemini(shortage_items: list[str], warehouse_items: list[str], api_key: str, model: str = 'gemini-2.5-flash') -> list[dict]:\\n  - For efficiency, batch multiple shortage items in one Gemini call\\n  - Send up to 10 shortage items at a time with the full warehouse list\\n  - Ask Gemini to match each shortage item to the best warehouse item\\n  - Returns list of match results\\n\\nThe Gemini prompt should be in Arabic and very specific:\\n- Focus on: اسم الصنف, التركيز, الشكل الدوائي, حجم العبوة\\n- Spelling differences are OK (the same drug with typos)\\n- Different concentrations = different product (NOT a match)\\n- Different forms (tablets vs syrup) = different product (NOT a match)\\n- Missing info (no concentration listed) = ambiguous, not an automatic match\\n\\nUse the google.genai SDK:\\n```python\\nfrom google import genai\\nclient = genai.Client(api_key=api_key)\\nresponse = client.models.generate_content(\\n    model=model,\\n    contents=prompt,\\n    config={'response_mime_type': 'application/json'}\\n)\\n```\\n\\n## 4. src/match/coordinator.py\\nThe main coordinator that orchestrates matching across all warehouses:\\n\\n```python\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Coordinator: matches shortages against all warehouses.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n```\\n\\nClass Coordinator:\\n- __init__(self, config: Config)\\n- process(self, shortage_items: list[dict], warehouse_data: dict[str, list[dict]]) -> dict:\\n  - warehouse_data maps warehouse_name -> list of items\\n  - For each warehouse (can think of each as a sub-agent):\\n    1. First pass: exact text matching (after normalization)\\n    2. Second pass: fuzzy matching with RapidFuzz for unmatched items\\n    3. Third pass: Gemini matching for remaining ambiguous cases\\n  - Track results per warehouse:\\n    - matched: list of (shortage_item, warehouse_item) confirmed matches\\n    - needs_review: ambiguous matches\\n  - After all warehouses processed:\\n    - Compile which shortages found in which warehouses\\n    - Identify shortages not found in any warehouse\\n  - Returns: {\\n      'warehouse_results': {name: {matched: [...], needs_review: [...]}},\\n      'not_found': [...],  # items not in any warehouse\\n      'summary': {total_shortages, matched_count, not_found_count, review_count}\\n    }\\n\\n- _match_warehouse(self, shortage_items, warehouse_items, warehouse_name) -> dict:\\n  - Process one warehouse (one sub-agent)\\n  - Print progress in Arabic\\n\\n## \n---\nThe checkpoint summary has been truncated due to hitting max length. Please see the conversation log file for the full conversation."}
{"step_index":148,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T15:59:23Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\"\"Pharmacy Drug Matching Pipeline\n\nMatches shortages with warehouse inventory using Gemini API.\nOutputs an Excel file with the results.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# Add project root to Python path\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\n\nfrom src.config import load_config\nfrom src.extract.file_handler import read_input_files\nfrom src.match.coordinator import Coordinator\nfrom src.output.excel_writer import write_results_excel\n\n\ndef main():\n    if hasattr(sys.stdout, \"reconfigure\"):\n        sys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Match drug shortages against warehouse catalogs\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--shortages\", \"-s\",\n        nargs=\"+\",\n        type=Path,\n        required=True,\n        help=\"Shortages files (Excel or PDF)\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--warehouses\", \"-w\",\n        nargs=\"+\",\n        type=Path,\n        required=True,\n        help=\"Warehouse files (Excel or PDF or JSON)\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--output\", \"-o\",\n        type=Path,\n        default=Path(\"output/results.xlsx\"),\n        help=\"Output Excel file path (default: output/results.xlsx)\",\n    )\n\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    for f in args.shortages + args.warehouses:\n        if not f.exists():\n            parser.error(f\"File not found: {f}\")\n\n    try:\n        config = load_config()\n    except ValueError as e:\n        print(f\"[!] {e}\")\n        print(\"Please copy .env.example to .env and fill in the keys.\")\n        return 1\n\n    print(f\"\\n[Settings]\")\n    print(f\"  Model: {config.gemini_model}\")\n    print(f\"  Unstructured API: {'OK' if config.unstructured_api_key else 'Missing'}\")\n    print(f\"  Gemini API: {'OK' if config.gemini_api_key else 'Missing'}\")\n\n    shortage_data = read_input_files(\n        args.shortages, role=\"shortages\", api_key=config.unstructured_api_key,\n    )\n\n    all_shortages = []\n    for filename, items in shortage_data.items():\n        all_shortages.extend(items)\n\n    if not all_shortages:\n        print(\"[!] No items found in shortages files!\")\n        return 1\n\n    print(f\"\\n[*] Total shortage items: {len(all_shortages)}\")\n\n    warehouse_data = read_input_files(\n        args.warehouses, role=\"warehouse\", api_key=config.unstructured_api_key,\n    )\n\n    if not warehouse_data:\n        print(\"[!] No items found in warehouse files!\")\n        return 1\n\n    coordinator = Coordinator(config)\n    results = coordinator.process(all_shortages, warehouse_data)\n\n    write_results_excel(results, args.output)\n\n    print(f\"\\n[+] Finished!\")\n    print(f\"    Results saved to: {args.output.resolve()}\")\n\n    summary = results.get(\"summary\", {})\n    if summary.get(\"not_found_count\", 0) > 0:\n        print(f\"    [!] {summary['not_found_count']} items NOT found in any warehouse\")\n    if summary.get(\"review_count\", 0) > 0:\n        print(f\"    [*] {summary['review_count']} items require manual review\")\n\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n","Description":"Translated prints in main.py to English to fix Powershell display issues","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\main.py","toolAction":"Translating main script","toolSummary":"Main.py translation"}}]}
